# A100 (compute capability 8.0 — the 80 GB and the 40 GB card alike) deployment parameters. Same shape and rules as configs/h100.env — this
# file pre-sets the one value that differs, the GPU this configuration targets, and takes everything else from h100.env (the mode still comes
# from `--mode` / CHAI1_OPT, the weights directory CHAI_DOWNLOADS_DIR from the caller's environment). Nothing here or in the kit reads the card's
# memory size: a 40 GB card runs the same code with the same levers as an 80 GB card, up to the crop its memory holds (README.md Notes, 'Other cards'; the reach lines below).
# usage: `run.sh pred|check|warm --config a100 [--mode <mode>] ...`, or `source configs/a100.env`. A GPU whose name does not contain A100
# is noted on the activation line, never refused. Per-card list — the ONLY differences from configs/h100.env; anything not named here runs
# the same code path with the same lever set as on the H100:
#  1. v4trimul (`fast` / `big`): the fused triangle multiplication asks the shared provider the mode's tier word (`fast` | `big`); the
#     provider's own table picks the row for compute capability 8.0 (no per-card table in this kit). Every other lever of the modes
#     (exact | fast | big, their implied tf32 / alloc included) has no per-GPU code; a call the provider refuses by name runs the trunk's own
#     statement, counted on the LEVER / EXIT lines, and an unexpected refusal ends the run `PAIRTRACK GATE REFUSED`, exit 1, naming the
#     lever — never a note at exit 0; `--mode off` or `--mode exact` is the way past it.
#  2. `exact` is byte-identical to `off` under `--det 1` through crop 1024 (inputs up to 1,024 tokens). At crops 1536 and 2048 stock's
#     TorchScript trunk runs a per-crop trace that chunks its linear layers and attention differently, and on sm80 the eager trunk's single
#     statement does not reproduce those two traces bit for bit (on sm90 it does): there `exact` is deterministic run to run but NOT
#     byte-identical to `off` — the same class of difference as `fast`. Use `off` when outputs above 1,024 tokens must equal stock's on an A100.
#  3. Reach on the 40 GB card (a deep MSA, ESM embeddings on): `off` and `big` fold through crop 1536, `exact` and `fast` through crop 1024
#     (their resident weights, resident ESM model and denoiser graph take memory stock's low-memory path does not); a larger crop ends with
#     CUDA's out-of-memory error on the item's `SEED FAIL` line, exit 1. Crop 2048 needs the 80 GB card in every mode, `off` included.
export MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU=${MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU:-A100}                                                            # compute capability 8.0
source "$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/h100.env"
